#: ../../../misc-devices/amd-sbi.rst:5
msgid "AMD SIDE BAND interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../misc-devices/amd-sbi.rst:7
msgid ""
"Some AMD Zen based processors supports system management functionality via "
"side-band interface (SBI) called Advanced Platform Management Link (APML). "
"APML is an I2C/I3C based 2-wire processor target interface. APML is used to "
"communicate with the Remote Management Interface (SB Remote Management "
"Interface (SB-RMI) and SB Temperature Sensor Interface (SB-TSI))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../misc-devices/amd-sbi.rst:15
msgid ""
"More details on the interface can be found in chapter \"5 Advanced Platform "
"Management Link (APML)\" of the family/model PPR [1]_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../misc-devices/amd-sbi.rst:18
msgid "https://docs.amd.com/v/u/en-US/55898_B1_pub_0_50"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../misc-devices/amd-sbi.rst:22
msgid "SBRMI device"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../misc-devices/amd-sbi.rst:24
msgid ""
"apml_sbrmi driver under the drivers/misc/amd-sbi creates miscdevice /dev/"
"sbrmi-* to let user space programs run APML mailbox, CPUID, MCAMSR and "
"register xfer commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../misc-devices/amd-sbi.rst:28
msgid ""
"Register sets is common across APML protocols. IOCTL is providing "
"synchronization among protocols as transactions may create race condition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../misc-devices/amd-sbi.rst:36
msgid ""
"apml_sbrmi driver registers hwmon sensors for monitoring power_cap_max, "
"current power consumption and managing power_cap."
msgstr ""

